# Bridges .env into the environment, so no .env parser has to exist in Swift.
#
# Decision D1 in docs/open-agent-plan.md: Swift cannot read .env files natively,
# and a hand-rolled parser is fifteen lines of the parts people get wrong —
# `export ` prefixes, `#` inside quoted values, CRLF, escapes. direnv already
# solves it, and every documented invocation of this project is a terminal
# command that inherits the shell environment for free.
#
# Requires `direnv allow` once, in this directory.
#
# The variable is TYPESAFE_API_KEY. TypeSafe is the vendor; Jev is the model
# (jev-1.13.0). There is no JEV_API_KEY — nothing here reads that name, and
# Credentials.apiKey() fails naming the one it wants.
dotenv
